---
---
<section id="install" class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="text-center mb-16 fade-in">
      <div class="badge mb-5">Get started</div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-text-primary tracking-tight mb-5">
        5 minutes to<br/><span class="text-cal-gold">your first question.</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="text-text-secondary text-lg max-w-xl mx-auto">
        No Docker, no server, no signup. Install it, paste a bCourses token, tell your AI app
        where it is.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">

      <!-- Steps 1 and 2 -->
      <div class="fade-in mb-12">
        <div class="terminal">
          <div class="terminal-header">
            <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#ff5f57]"></div>
            <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#febc2e]"></div>
            <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#28c840]"></div>
            <span class="ml-3 text-xs text-text-muted font-sans">Terminal</span>
          </div>
          <div class="terminal-body text-[13px] md:text-sm space-y-1.5">
            <div><span class="text-text-secondary">$</span> <span class="text-text-primary">uv tool install git+https://github.com/qazybekb/openmind.git</span></div>
            <div><span class="text-text-secondary">$</span> <span class="text-text-primary">openmind setup</span></div>
            <div class="mt-3 text-text-secondary">Paste your bCourses access token.</div>
            <div class="text-text-muted">It is stored in your operating system's credential store, not in a file.</div>
            <div>&ensp;<span class="text-text-secondary">bCourses token:</span> ********</div>
            <div>&ensp;<span class="text-text-muted">Token: 1072~****4T2r</span></div>
            <div>&ensp;<span class="text-green-500">Connected as Oski Bear (America/Los_Angeles).</span></div>
            <div class="mt-2 text-text-secondary">Your active courses (* = current term):</div>
            <div>&ensp;<span class="text-text-muted">1. * Causal Inference&ensp;[Fall 2026]&ensp;(id 1001)</span></div>
            <div>&ensp;<span class="text-text-muted">2. * Natural Language Processing&ensp;[Fall 2026]&ensp;(id 1002)</span></div>
            <div>&ensp;<span class="text-text-muted">3. &nbsp;&nbsp;Social Issues of Information&ensp;[Spring 2026]&ensp;(id 1003)</span></div>
            <div class="mt-1 text-text-secondary">OpenMind shares only the courses you choose here with your AI app.</div>
            <div>&ensp;<span class="text-text-secondary">Numbers to share; Enter for the 2 current; 'all' for all:</span> <span class="text-text-primary">1,2</span></div>
            <div class="mt-2"><span class="text-green-500">Saved 2 courses.</span> <span class="text-text-muted">11,156 courses across 240 subjects indexed.</span></div>
            <div class="mt-2 text-text-muted">Course materials are NOT stored locally unless you ask for it.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-text-muted text-xs mt-3">
          PyPI publication is pending. After the corrected release is published,
          <code class="text-text-secondary">uv tool install openmind-berkeley</code> is an alternative.
          From a local checkout, use <code class="text-text-secondary">uv tool install .</code>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 3: connect the host -->
      <div class="fade-in fade-in-delay-1 mb-12">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-text-primary mb-2">Then connect your AI app</h3>
        <p class="text-text-secondary text-xs mb-5">
          <code class="text-text-secondary">openmind mcp</code> prints the exact config for each app,
          with the absolute path filled in. Nothing secret appears in it.
        </p>
        <div class="terminal">
          <div class="terminal-header">
            <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#ff5f57]"></div>
            <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#febc2e]"></div>
            <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#28c840]"></div>
            <span class="ml-3 text-xs text-text-muted font-sans">claude_desktop_config.json</span>
          </div>
          <div class="terminal-body text-[13px] space-y-0.5">
            <div><span class="text-text-secondary">&#123;</span></div>
            <div>&ensp;<span class="text-cal-gold">"mcpServers"</span><span class="text-text-secondary">: &#123;</span></div>
            <div>&ensp;&ensp;<span class="text-cal-gold">"openmind"</span><span class="text-text-secondary">: &#123; </span><span class="text-cal-gold">"command"</span><span class="text-text-secondary">: </span><span class="text-text-primary">"/Users/you/.local/bin/openmind-mcp"</span><span class="text-text-secondary"> &#125;</span></div>
            <div>&ensp;<span class="text-text-secondary">&#125;</span></div>
            <div><span class="text-text-secondary">&#125;</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-text-muted text-xs mt-3">
          Claude Code: <code class="text-text-secondary">claude mcp add --scope user openmind -- /path/to/openmind-mcp</code><br/>
          Cursor: the same JSON block in <code class="text-text-secondary">~/.cursor/mcp.json</code>.
          ChatGPT desktop: add a local (STDIO) server with that command.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- What you need -->
      <div class="fade-in fade-in-delay-2 mb-12">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-text-primary mb-5">What you need</h3>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
          <a href="/guides/bcourses/" class="card group">
            <div class="text-lg mb-2">&#x1f4d8;</div>
            <h4 class="text-text-primary font-medium text-sm mb-1 group-hover:text-cal-gold transition-colors">A bCourses token</h4>
            <p class="text-text-secondary text-xs">Account &rarr; Settings &rarr; New Access Token</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/guides/connect/" class="card group">
            <div class="text-lg mb-2">&#x1f5a5;</div>
            <h4 class="text-text-primary font-medium text-sm mb-1 group-hover:text-cal-gold transition-colors">A desktop AI app</h4>
            <p class="text-text-secondary text-xs">Claude, Cursor, or ChatGPT &mdash; the desktop version</p>
          </a>
          <a href="https://github.com/qazybekb/openmind/blob/main/docs/SETUP.md" target="_blank" class="card group">
            <div class="text-lg mb-2">&#x1f40d;</div>
            <h4 class="text-text-primary font-medium text-sm mb-1 group-hover:text-cal-gold transition-colors">Python 3.11+</h4>
            <p class="text-text-secondary text-xs">macOS, Windows, or Linux</p>
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="text-center text-text-muted text-xs mt-4">
          <a href="/guides/" class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-text-secondary">Step-by-step guides &rarr;</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Optional extras -->
      <div class="fade-in fade-in-delay-3 mb-12">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-text-primary mb-2">Optional, later</h3>
        <p class="text-text-secondary text-xs mb-5">
          By default OpenMind sees the <em>names</em> of your files, not what's inside them.
          Indexing a course extracts its text into a private file on your machine so tutoring can
          quote it with page citations.
        </p>
        <div class="terminal">
          <div class="terminal-header">
            <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#ff5f57]"></div>
            <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#febc2e]"></div>
            <div class="terminal-dot bg-[#28c840]"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="terminal-body text-[13px] space-y-1">
            <div><span class="text-text-secondary">$</span> openmind <span class="text-text-primary">index --course 1001</span> <span class="text-text-secondary">&ensp;# search inside slides and readings</span></div>
            <div><span class="text-text-secondary">$</span> openmind <span class="text-text-primary">doctor</span> <span class="text-text-secondary">&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;# check everything end to end</span></div>
            <div><span class="text-text-secondary">$</span> openmind <span class="text-text-primary">update-data</span> <span class="text-text-secondary">&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;# refresh the Berkeley catalog</span></div>
            <div><span class="text-text-secondary">$</span> openmind <span class="text-text-primary">config</span> <span class="text-text-secondary">&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;# show or change settings</span></div>
            <div><span class="text-text-secondary">$</span> openmind <span class="text-text-primary">clear --all</span> <span class="text-text-secondary">&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;&ensp;# delete everything it stores</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
